=== Comprehensive Utility Classes ===

Rudiments provides a wide range of utility classes.

* '''Standard Input and Output'''
 * [programming/stdio.html Using the standard I/O classes]
* '''Sleeping'''
 * [programming/snooze.html Using the snooze class]
* '''Process and Process Environment'''
 * [programming/process.html Using the process class]
 * [programming/commandline.html Using the commandline class]
 * [programming/environment.html Using the environment class]
* '''Character and String Manipulation'''
 * [programming/character.html Using the character class]
 * [programming/charstring.html Using the charstring class]
* '''Binary Data Manipulation'''
 * [programming/bytestring.html Using the bytestring class]
* '''Regular Expressions'''
 * [programming/regularexpression.html Using the regularexpression class]
* '''Random Numbers'''
 * [programming/randomnumber.html Using the randomnumber class]
* '''Encryption'''
 * [programming/crypt.html Using the crypt class]
* '''Date and Time'''
 * [programming/datetime.html Using the datetime class]
* '''System Information'''
 * [programming/error.html Using the error class]
 * [programming/sys.html Using the sys class]
 * [programming/userentry.html Using the userentry class]
 * [programming/groupentry.html Using the groupentry class]
 * [programming/hostentry.html Using the hostentry class]
 * [programming/protocolentry.html Using the protocolentry class]
 * [programming/serviceentry.html Using the serviceentry class]
* '''Files, File Permissions, Directories and Filesystems'''
 * [programming/file.html Using the file class]
 * [programming/permissions.html Using the permissions class]
 * [programming/directory.html Using the directory class]
 * [programming/memorymap.html Using the memorymap class]
 * [programming/filesystem.html Using the filesystem class]
* '''Interprocess Communication'''
 * [programming/sharedmemory.html Using the sharedmemory class]
 * [programming/semaphoreset.html Using the semaphoreset class]
 * [programming/signal.html Using the signal classes]
* '''Parameter Strings'''
 * [programming/parameterstring.html Using the parameterstring class]
* '''XML'''
 * [programming/xmldom.html Using the xmldom and domnode classes]
 * [programming/xmlsax.html Using the xmlsax class]
* '''Logging'''
 * [programming/logger.html Using the logger class]
* '''Dynamic Libraries'''
 * [programming/dynamiclib.html Using the dynamiclib class]

